      "content": "Even if you feel generally okay, excessive thirst and urination are significant symptoms that need medical evaluation, not just ignored. While increased water intake is generally good, it won't address the underlying cause of highly concentrated urine or constant thirst. Given your Type 2 diabetes, it is much safer to call your doctor's office and explain the urgency of the symptoms, even if you wait until the weekend. Please prioritize speaking with a healthcare provider about these changes.",
